  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An improved digital environment and physical environment to support effective and efficient operations and safe and sustainable workplaces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the agile approach necessary to enabling a forward-thinking culture, the ILO creates new digital solutions and skills to improve stakeholder collaboration and decision-making and generate efficiencies in time-critical amendments processing, thereby enhancing the effectiveness of the important work undertaken during sessions of the International Labour Conference. Efficiencies are further generated through the mainstreaming of AI tools into the workplace to facilitate the drafting and summarizing of documents, emails, meeting minutes and presentations, as well as the production of publications and communication materials.
The ILO continues to transform the workplace by providing safe and sustainable office spaces that enable innovative and collaborative work. Taking advantage of opportunities offered by teleworking, the Office achieved space savings and reduced its overall footprint. In response to an increasingly unstable security environment, the Office enhanced the implementation and coordination of its security policy at headquarters and in field locations. Acknowledging the urgency of climate action, the Office is reducing its ecological footprint, promoting sustainable practices and collaborating with local stakeholders to embed sustainability in its organizational fabric.</narrative>
  </description>
